{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'type ReviewDraftCriterion|type ReviewCriterionMapping|mappings.*not-applicable|not-applicable.*mappings' pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_*go pose-mcp/internal/cli\"","aggregated_output":"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_rounds.go:64:type ReviewDraftCriterion struct {\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_brief.go:117:const briefRulesTextV5 = \"POSE checks the conclusion before it records it, and refuses the whole draft when one rule breaks: (a) a `passed` criterion of kind judgment carries a `rationale` saying what you examined and what you concluded; (b) the `evidence` of a `passed` criterion is exactly one of the refs listed under Sealed evidence (`<class>:<id>`, of a class the criterion asks for when it names one), never a file and line, a command or a structural fact id: those go in a finding or in the `rationale`; (c) a criterion disposed `finding` carries as its `evidence` the `id` of a finding listed in `findings`, and that finding is open until you give it `action`, `owner` and `review_by`; (d) each structural fact listed above is answered by the criterion that asks for structural mapping, as its `mappings`: `[{\\\"delta\\\": <fact id>, \\\"basis\\\": <requirement or decision ref>, \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"mapped\\\", \\\"rationale\\\": <why>}]`, or `not-applicable` with the reason; (e) a `not-applicable` carries a `rationale` and is refused when the bundle seals evidence of a class the criterion asks for; (f) every required criterion and every tool above is answered; (g) the `disposition` of a tool is `passed`, `failed`, `not-used` or `deferred`, never anything else (`not-run` is refused); a tool listed as required must be run and `passed`, with the ref of the sealed evidence it produced as `evidence` when it names classes, and `not-used` is accepted for a required tool only when the plan says no producer exists; a recommended tool you did not run is `not-used` with a `rationale`; (h) the `evidence` of a tool is `<class>:<ref>`: when the tool lists evidence classes, a ref of one of them that the bundle sealed (listed under Sealed evidence), otherwise `command:` followed by the command you ran; a bare command line is refused; (i) a draft that approves leaves no finding open: each finding is either a follow-up with `action`, `owner` and `review_by`, which is recorded as an accepted risk, or the draft requests changes; a finding without them is open and the approval is refused.\"\npose-mcp/internal/pose/review_closeout.go:353:type ReviewCriterionMapping struct {\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
