y this CLI/ledger diff.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The scan reported incomplete coverage because two unrelated specs were invalid/unreadable and one uncovered marker; this is not evidence of a defect in the reviewed change.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"closeout-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Completion-only check: the spec is in-progress and this review explicitly forbids recording an attestation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"review-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Completion-only check: no attestation may be recorded in this run. The command also reports the current review as unapproved.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"suggest-review\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"surface-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The command returned zero findings for the composed capability; sealed component integration evidence covers the delegate surface.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Both current strict validation invocations failed before checks could execute because the read-only sandbox denied Go build-workdir/cache writes. The sealed bundle provides passing global build, e2e, integration and unit evidence; focused changed-package tests and vet also passed in this run.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The module validation rerun was blocked by the same read-only Go workdir/cache restriction; the sealed bundle contains the module build, e2e, integration and unit passes, and focused tests/vet passed here.\\\"}\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_DRAFT'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'FINAL_REVIEW' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\nThe change addresses the session-escape cause with a per-run marker and keeps old run/receipt schemas, but R5 still has a crash window before the active marker and `delegate ls` omits the stalled attempt'\"'s cause. The Linux reaper can signal a reused PID and silently treat \"'`/proc` read failures as successful cleanup. The manuals also overstate non-Linux behavior.\n\nFindings:\n- N1 high — [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:716): a crash after reservation but before active-marker publication leaves an unlisted reservation that blocks later dispatches.\n- N2 medium — [delegation_list.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go:168): stalled listings omit the abandonment cause required by R5.\n- N3 medium — [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:74): PID reuse between inspection and signal can kill a process outside this run.\n- N4 high — [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:38): unreadable `/proc` entries are treated as no leftovers, allowing cleanup while a child survives.\n- N5 low — [POSE.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/POSE.md:1078): the manual claims environment-marked reaping without the Linux-only qualification in L2.\n\nRules applied: mixed bugfix/documentation change; `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. I consulted the delegation round 4 and round 5 handoffs; recurrence scan flagged no keys.\n\nChecks: focused `go test` and `go vet` passed; `surface-check` passed. Strict global and module validation were blocked before checks executed because the read-only sandbox denied Go build-workdir/cache writes. The bundle contains passing build/e2e/integration/unit evidence. The working tree remains clean.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":716,\"summary\":\"The reservation is published before the active marker. A dispatch stopped in that gap leaves a reservation with no run or marker, so delegate ls cannot expose it and later admission remains blocked.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go\",\"line\":168,\"summary\":\"A stalled attempt is listed with only its state and timestamp; the abandonment cause required by R5 is omitted from both text and JSON projections.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\"line\":74,\"summary\":\"The process is identified by numeric PID and later signaled by PID without pinning process identity; if it exits and the PID is reused between inspection and SIGKILL, an unrelated process can be killed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\"line\":38,\"summary\":\"The /proc scan treats ReadDir failure as an empty process set, skips unreadable environ files, and treats stat read failures as process exit; a leftover can survive while the dispatcher reports successful reaping and proceeds to cleanup.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"POSE.md\",\"line\":1078,\"summary\":\"The manual claims environment-marked process reaping without limiting the claim to Linux; review_reap_other.go is a no-op and the spec records process-group-only cleanup on other platforms.\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\",\"rationale\":\"Verified: dispatch passes the run'\"'s sealed-checkout path to the adapter environment, Linux excludes its own PID, and abandoned release requires a dead owner. Unresolved: /proc visibility and PID identity can change between inspection and signal, and the reservation precedes marker publication (N1, N3, N4). Accepted spec limits: a process that clears the marker escapes (L1), and non-Linux cleanup remains process-group-only (L2); the manual's omission of L2 is N5.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-observability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N4\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"compatibility\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The release writes the existing version-1 ReviewRun and attempt-receipt formats; earlier records retain their parser and meaning. I checked the run ledger and delegate list projections.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"correctness\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"design-causality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"D1 addresses the observed session-escape cause by finding processes with the run-specific sealed-checkout entry and doing so after adapter/group termination but before cleanup inventory. D2 uses the existing failed-run and receipt records so older readers retain ordinary failed-run semantics. The design assessment reports no structural deltas; N1, N3, and N4 identify conditions where this design does not complete its promised lifecycle.\\\",\\\"mappings\\\":[]},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"documentation\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N5\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"I compared the root and scaffold manuals in both locales with the Linux and non-Linux implementations and the spec's L2 limit.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"operability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"requirements\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The change stays within the stated dispatcher, attempt ledger, brief and manual scope; the design assessment found no structural deltas.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N3\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Process-group-only cleanup is the smallest change but misses commands in their own sessions, so D1's per-run marker scan is a proportionate extension. D2 reuses the existing failed-run and receipt contract rather than adding a new ledger schema. The negative space is explicit: cleared markers and non-Linux platforms remain outside the guarantee (L1/L2); procfs denial and PID reuse are concrete invalidation conditions recorded as N3/N4.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The command exited 0. Its output reported 19 claims and 25 observed artifacts, plus repository-wide orphan warnings; it named a change-set head e7873d1414a8 rather than the brief's be42f2eff3ce, so I kept the sealed brief's range as the review subject.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-design\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The design assessment returned no deltas and matches the sealed structure evidence.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-discover\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess integrate --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The scan completed and reported three unobserved HTTP consumers; none is a boundary changed by this CLI/ledger diff.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The scan reported incomplete coverage because two unrelated specs were invalid/unreadable and one uncovered marker; this is not evidence of a defect in the reviewed change.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"closeout-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Completion-only check: the spec is in-progress and this review explicitly forbids recording an attestation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"review-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Completion-only check: no attestation may be recorded in this run. The command also reports the current review as unapproved.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"suggest-review\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"surface-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The command returned zero findings for the composed capability; sealed component integration evidence covers the delegate surface.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Both current strict validation invocations failed before checks could execute because the read-only sandbox denied Go build-workdir/cache writes. The sealed bundle provides passing global build, e2e, integration and unit evidence; focused changed-package tests and vet also passed in this run.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The module validation rerun was blocked by the same read-only Go workdir/cache restriction; the sealed bundle contains the module build, e2e, integration and unit passes, and focused tests/vet passed here.\\\"}\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nFINAL_REVIEW'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'FINAL_REVIEW' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\nThe change addresses the session-escape cause with a per-run marker and keeps old run/receipt schemas, but R5 still has a crash window before the active marker and `delegate ls` omits the stalled attempt'\"'s cause. The Linux reaper can signal a reused PID and silently treat \"'`/proc` read failures as successful cleanup. The manuals also overstate non-Linux behavior.\n\nFindings:\n- N1 high — [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:716): a crash after reservation but before active-marker publication leaves an unlisted reservation that blocks later dispatches.\n- N2 medium — [delegation_list.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go:168): stalled listings omit the abandonment cause required by R5.\n- N3 medium — [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:74): PID reuse between inspection and signal can kill a process outside this run.\n- N4 high — [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:38): unreadable `/proc` entries are treated as no leftovers, allowing cleanup while a child survives.\n- N5 low — [POSE.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/POSE.md:1078): the manual claims environment-marked reaping without the Linux-only qualification in L2.\n\nRules applied: mixed bugfix/documentation change; `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. I consulted the delegation round 4 and round 5 handoffs; recurrence scan flagged no keys.\n\nChecks: focused `go test` and `go vet` passed; `surface-check` passed. Strict global and module validation were blocked before checks executed because the read-only sandbox denied Go build-workdir/cache writes. The bundle contains passing build/e2e/integration/unit evidence. The working tree remains clean.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":716,\"summary\":\"The reservation is published before the active marker. A dispatch stopped in that gap leaves a reservation with no run or marker, so delegate ls cannot expose it and later admission remains blocked.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go\",\"line\":168,\"summary\":\"A stalled attempt is listed with only its state and timestamp; the abandonment cause required by R5 is omitted from both text and JSON projections.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\"line\":74,\"summary\":\"The process is identified by numeric PID and later signaled by PID without pinning process identity; if it exits and the PID is reused between inspection and SIGKILL, an unrelated process can be killed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\"line\":38,\"summary\":\"The /proc scan treats ReadDir failure as an empty process set, skips unreadable environ files, and treats stat read failures as process exit; a leftover can survive while the dispatcher reports successful reaping and proceeds to cleanup.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"POSE.md\",\"line\":1078,\"summary\":\"The manual claims environment-marked process reaping without limiting the claim to Linux; review_reap_other.go is a no-op and the spec records process-group-only cleanup on other platforms.\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\",\"rationale\":\"Verified: dispatch passes the run'\"'s sealed-checkout path to the adapter environment, Linux excludes its own PID, and abandoned release requires a dead owner. Unresolved: /proc visibility and PID identity can change between inspection and signal, and the reservation precedes marker publication (N1, N3, N4). Accepted spec limits: a process that clears the marker escapes (L1), and non-Linux cleanup remains process-group-only (L2); the manual's omission of L2 is N5.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-contracts\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"backend-observability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N4\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"compatibility\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The release writes the existing version-1 ReviewRun and attempt-receipt formats; earlier records retain their parser and meaning. I checked the run ledger and delegate list projections.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"correctness\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"design-causality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"D1 addresses the observed session-escape cause by finding processes with the run-specific sealed-checkout entry and doing so after adapter/group termination but before cleanup inventory. D2 uses the existing failed-run and receipt records so older readers retain ordinary failed-run semantics. The design assessment reports no structural deltas; N1, N3, and N4 identify conditions where this design does not complete its promised lifecycle.\\\",\\\"mappings\\\":[]},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"documentation\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N5\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"I compared the root and scaffold manuals in both locales with the Linux and non-Linux implementations and the spec's L2 limit.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"operability\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N2\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"requirements\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N1\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"scope\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The change stays within the stated dispatcher, attempt ledger, brief and manual scope; the design assessment found no structural deltas.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"security\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"N3\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Process-group-only cleanup is the smallest change but misses commands in their own sessions, so D1's per-run marker scan is a proportionate extension. D2 reuses the existing failed-run and receipt contract rather than adding a new ledger schema. The negative space is explicit: cleared markers and non-Linux platforms remain outside the guarantee (L1/L2); procfs denial and PID reuse are concrete invalidation conditions recorded as N3/N4.\\\"}\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"artifact-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The command exited 0. Its output reported 19 claims and 25 observed artifacts, plus repository-wide orphan warnings; it named a change-set head e7873d1414a8 rather than the brief's be42f2eff3ce, so I kept the sealed brief's range as the review subject.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-design\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The design assessment returned no deltas and matches the sealed structure evidence.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-discover\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-integrate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess integrate --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The scan completed and reported three unobserved HTTP consumers; none is a boundary changed by this CLI/ledger diff.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"failed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The scan reported incomplete coverage because two unrelated specs were invalid/unreadable and one uncovered marker; this is not evidence of a defect in the reviewed change.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"closeout-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Completion-only check: the spec is in-progress and this review explicitly forbids recording an attestation.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"review-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"deferred\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Completion-only check: no attestation may be recorded in this run. The command also reports the current review as unapproved.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"suggest-review\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"surface-check\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The command returned zero findings for the composed capability; sealed component integration evidence covers the delegate surface.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Both current strict validation invocations failed before checks could execute because the read-only sandbox denied Go build-workdir/cache writes. The sealed bundle provides passing global build, e2e, integration and unit evidence; focused changed-package tests and vet also passed in this run.\\\"},\n    {\\\"id\\\":\\\"validate\\\",\\\"component\\\":\\\"pose-mcp\\\",\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"passed\\\",\\\"evidence\\\":\\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The module validation rerun was blocked by the same read-only Go workdir/cache restriction; the sealed bundle contains the module build, e2e, integration and unit passes, and focused tests/vet passed here.\\\"}\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nFINAL_REVIEW'","aggregated_output":"Draft check: the conclusion step would accept this draft.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nThe change addresses the session-escape cause with a per-run marker and keeps old run and receipt schemas. R5 still has a crash window before the active marker, and `delegate ls` omits the stalled attempt’s cause. The Linux reaper can signal a reused PID, silently treat `/proc` read failures as successful cleanup, and the manuals overstate non-Linux behavior.\n\nFindings:\n\n- **N1 — High:** [review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:716) publishes the reservation before the active marker. A crash in that gap leaves an unlisted reservation that blocks later dispatches.\n- **N2 — Medium:** [delegation_list.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go:168) lists stalled attempts without the abandonment cause required by R5.\n- **N3 — Medium:** [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:74) signals by PID after inspecting it without pinning process identity. PID reuse could lead it to kill a process outside this run.\n- **N4 — High:** [review_reap_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go:38) treats `/proc` scan failures as an empty process set, allowing cleanup to proceed while a leftover process survives.\n- **N5 — Low:** [POSE.md](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-563042235/worktree/POSE.md:1078) describes environment-marked reaping without the Linux-only qualification in L2.\n\n**Checks:** Focused Go tests and `go vet` passed; `surface-check` passed. Global and module strict validation could not execute checks because the read-only sandbox denied Go build-workdir and cache writes. The sealed bundle contains passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. The artifact check exited 0, but reported a change-set head different from the brief’s; the sealed brief remains the review subject. The working tree is clean.\n\n**Rules applied:** Mixed bugfix/documentation change; `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. I consulted the delegation round 4 and round 5 handoffs; the recurrence scan flagged no keys.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go\",\"line\":716,\"summary\":\"The reservation is published before the active marker. A dispatch stopped in that gap leaves a reservation with no run or marker, so delegate ls cannot expose it and later admission remains blocked.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/delegation_list.go\",\"line\":168,\"summary\":\"A stalled attempt is listed with only its state and timestamp; the abandonment cause required by R5 is omitted from both text and JSON projections.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\"line\":74,\"summary\":\"The process is identified by numeric PID and later signaled by PID without pinning process identity; if it exits and the PID is reused between inspection and SIGKILL, an unrelated process can be killed.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"high\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_linux.go\",\"line\":38,\"summary\":\"The /proc scan treats ReadDir failure as an empty process set, skips unreadable environ files, and treats stat read failures as process exit; a leftover can survive while the dispatcher reports successful reaping and proceeds to cleanup.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"POSE.md\",\"line\":1078,\"summary\":\"The manual claims environment-marked process reaping without limiting the claim to Linux; review_reap_other.go is a no-op and the spec records process-group-only cleanup on other platforms.\"}\n  ],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\",\"rationale\":\"Verified: dispatch passes the run's sealed-checkout path to the adapter environment, Linux excludes its own PID, and abandoned release requires a dead owner. Unresolved: /proc visibility and PID identity can change between inspection and signal, and the reservation precedes marker publication (N1, N3, N4). Accepted spec limits: a process that clears the marker escapes (L1), and non-Linux cleanup remains process-group-only (L2); the manual's omission of L2 is N5.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\"},\n    {\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N4\"},\n    {\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegated-attempt-ledger-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The release writes the existing version-1 ReviewRun and attempt-receipt formats; earlier records retain their parser and meaning. I checked the run ledger and delegate list projections.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\",\"rationale\":\"D1 addresses the observed session-escape cause by finding processes with the run-specific sealed-checkout entry and doing so after adapter/group termination but before cleanup inventory. D2 uses the existing failed-run and receipt records so older readers retain ordinary failed-run semantics. The design assessment reports no structural deltas; N1, N3, and N4 identify conditions where this design does not complete its promised lifecycle.\",\"mappings\":[]},\n    {\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N5\",\"rationale\":\"I compared the root and scaffold manuals in both locales with the Linux and non-Linux implementations and the spec's L2 limit.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N2\"},\n    {\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n    {\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\",\"rationale\":\"The change stays within the stated dispatcher, attempt ledger, brief and manual scope; the design assessment found no structural deltas.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N3\"},\n    {\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\",\"rationale\":\"Process-group-only cleanup is the smallest change but misses commands in their own sessions, so D1's per-run marker scan is a proportionate extension. D2 reuses the existing failed-run and receipt contract rather than adding a new ledger schema. The negative space is explicit: cleared markers and non-Linux platforms remain outside the guarantee (L1/L2); procfs denial and PID reuse are concrete invalidation conditions recorded as N3/N4.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes --strict\",\"rationale\":\"The command exited 0. Its output reported 19 claims and 25 observed artifacts, plus repository-wide orphan warnings; it named a change-set head e7873d1414a8 rather than the brief's be42f2eff3ce, so I kept the sealed brief's range as the review subject.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-c71f902ab6e6920d\",\"rationale\":\"The design assessment returned no deltas and matches the sealed structure evidence.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess integrate --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The scan completed and reported three unobserved HTTP consumers; none is a boundary changed by this CLI/ledger diff.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"failed\",\"evidence\":\"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The scan reported incomplete coverage because two unrelated specs were invalid/unreadable and one uncovered marker; this is not evidence of a defect in the reviewed change.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" closeout-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\"rationale\":\"Completion-only check: the spec is in-progress and this review explicitly forbids recording an attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" review-check spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes\",\"rationale\":\"Completion-only check: no attestation may be recorded in this run. The command also reports the current review as unapproved.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:\\\"$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n    {\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delegation-surface-integration\",\"rationale\":\"The command returned zero findings for the composed capability; sealed component integration evidence covers the delegate surface.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\"rationale\":\"Both current strict validation invocations failed before checks could execute because the read-only sandbox denied Go build-workdir/cache writes. The sealed bundle provides passing global build, e2e, integration and unit evidence; focused changed-package tests and vet also passed in this run.\"},\n    {\"id\":\"validate\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The module validation rerun was blocked by the same read-only Go workdir/cache restriction; the sealed bundle contains the module build, e2e, integration and unit passes, and focused tests/vet passed here.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
